  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 101 AM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nTypical for an El Nino year, there is a split jet with the\nsouthern stream sitting across the U.S./Mexico border this week.\nThus even though the air behind the cold front is unusually cold,\nthere will be no ridge moving in to increase temperatures. Temps\nbehind the front will be below normal and a slow increase through\nnext week will only get the back to normal by next Wednesday.\n\nIt will be mostly dry next week, with the exception of this\nweekend when a second low moves into the central plains. Lift from\nthe low and an associated jet max over West Texas will create\nscattered showers to form mainly in the Big Bend though a few\nstrays could reach as far north as the I-20 corridor. Little\nrainfall is expected from this activity before drier air returns\nnext week.\n\nHennig",
